<title>ISRAEL: Israel approves Teva's Copaxone drug.</title>
<headline>Israel approves Teva's Copaxone drug.</headline>
<dateline>TEL AVIV 1996-11-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Israel's Health Ministry has given Teva Pharmaceutical Industries approval to market its multiple sclerosis treatment Copaxone, the company announced on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Teva said it received the approval on Tuesday night. Israel is the first country to approve the sale of the new drug. Teva expects to begin marketing the drug in Israel before the end of the year.</p>
<p>The drug is in the final stages of receiving approval from the U.S. Food &amp; Drug Administration. Most analysts expect final approval to be granted by the end of the year.</p>
<p>Teva, which is also traded on Nasdaq, is Israel's largest drug company.</p>
<p>- Tel Aviv newsroom, 972-3-537-2211</p>
</text>
